# Neo Shift parameters (docs/specs/neo-shift.md). The order changes only with a version (machines.md §3.2): songs and presets
# store values by position; new parameters are appended. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoShift
namespace NeoBuzz.Shift
class NeoShiftMachine
tracks 1
summary Pitch shifter, frequency shifter and ring modulator in one effect. Pitch moves every partial by the same ratio (-24 to +24 semitones and cents) with a two-tap delay-line shifter (Fast, a Window of 10 to 100 ms sets its latency and smoothness) or a phase-locked phase vocoder (Smooth, 2047 samples of latency) and a stereo detune for doubling. Frequency moves every partial by the same number of hertz (-2000 to +2000 Hz, a single sideband) with a feedback for the rising or falling barber-pole and a Spread that shifts the right side the other way. Ring multiplies the sound by a carrier of 1 Hz to 5 kHz (sine, triangle or square, band-limited) with a Depth from amplitude modulation to full ring. Notes in can set the pitch shift (against a Root) or the carrier. Low and High cut on the wet path, Mix and Amount (0 and Mix 0 are bit-exact dry). Use it for octaves, fifths, doubling, metallic bells, throbbing tremolo and endless rising or falling echoes.

group Mode
Mode        "Mode"          0 2 0       enum Pitch Frequency Ring                    | What the effect does: pitch shift, frequency shift or ring modulation
    how Chooses between moving all partials by a ratio, moving all partials by a number of hertz, or multiplying the sound by a carrier.
    sound Pitch keeps the harmonics in tune, Frequency bends them into bell-like or barber-pole tones, Ring adds the sum and difference of the sound and the carrier.
group Pitch
Pitch       "Pitch"         0 48 12     int -24 st signed                            | Pitch shift in semitones, -24 to +24
    id pitch
    how Sets the shift in whole semitones.
    sound Seven up is a fifth above, twelve up an octave, twelve down an octave below.
Fine        "Fine"          0 200 100   int -100 cents signed                        | Fine pitch shift in cents, added to the semitones
    id fine
    how Adds a fine shift in cents (a hundredth of a semitone) to the semitones.
    sound A few cents against the dry sound make a slow chorus-like beat.
Quality     "Quality"       0 1 0       enum Fast Smooth                             | Fast: a two-tap delay-line shifter, latency half the Window. Smooth: a phase-locked phase vocoder, 2047 samples of latency
    id quality
    how Chooses the delay-line shifter (Fast, short latency, a slight warble on low notes) or the phase vocoder (Smooth, clean on chords and pads, a longer latency).
    sound Fast is tight and a little rough on low notes, Smooth stays clear on chords and held notes but follows a fast attack a little late.
Window      "Window"        0 90 30     lin 10 100 ms 0                                 | Fast: the length of the shifter's window, 10 to 100 ms; also its latency (half of it)
    id window
    how Sets the window of the Fast shifter; a longer window is smoother on low notes, a shorter one is tighter.
    sound Short windows add a fast flutter to low notes, long ones smear attacks and add delay.
Detune      "Stereo detune" 0 50 0      int 0 cents                                  | The left side is shifted down and the right side up by this many cents, for doubling
    id stereo_detune
    how Shifts the left channel down and the right channel up by this many cents.
    sound A few cents widen the sound into a double; more makes it seasick.
group Frequency
Shift       "Shift"         0 4000 2000 int -2000 Hz signed                          | Frequency shift in hertz, -2000 to +2000: every partial moves by the same number of hertz
    id shift
    how Moves every frequency of the sound up (or down) by the same number of hertz.
    sound A few hertz make a slow phasing, tens of hertz bend a voice into a metallic one, hundreds make bells.
ShiftFine   "Shift fine"    0 1000 500  lin -5 5 Hz 2                                | Fine frequency shift in hertz, added to Shift
    id shift_fine
    how Adds a fine shift of up to 5 Hz to Shift, in steps of 0.01 Hz.
    sound Fractions of a hertz give the slowest phasing there is.
Feedback    "Feedback"      0 1000 500  lin -95 95 % 0                               | Share of the shifted sound fed back in: positive rises, negative falls (-95 to +95 %)
    id feedback
    how Feeds the shifted sound back into the shifter, so each repeat moves again.
    sound Positive values make a rising barber-pole, negative values a falling one; high values ring on.
Spread      "Spread"        0 1000 0    pct                                          | The right side is shifted the other way by this share of the shift
    id spread
    how Shifts the right channel by the opposite amount (100 % = the left and right shifts mirror each other).
    sound Left rises while the right falls: a wide, swirling stereo image.
group Ring
Carrier     "Carrier"       0 6000 4286 freq 1 5000                                  | Carrier frequency, 1 Hz to 5 kHz
    id carrier
    how Sets the frequency of the oscillator the sound is multiplied with.
    sound Below 20 Hz it is a tremolo, in the audio range it adds sum and difference tones: metal, bells, robots.
Shape       "Shape"         0 2 0       enum Sine Triangle Square                    | The carrier's shape (triangle and square are band-limited)
    id shape
    how Chooses the carrier's waveform.
    sound Sine gives two clean sidebands, triangle and square add more, brighter ones.
Depth       "Depth"         0 1000 1000 pct                                          | 0 % = amplitude modulation (the sound keeps its own level), 100 % = ring modulation (only the sidebands)
    id depth
    how Blends from amplitude modulation (the original stays) to ring modulation (the original is gone).
    sound At 0 % the sound is only tremolo-ed, at 100 % it is replaced by sum and difference tones.
group Notes
Follow      "Follow notes"  0 1 0       switch                                       | Notes set the effect: the pitch shift in Pitch mode (note minus Root), the carrier in Ring mode
    id follow_notes
    how Lets the notes sent to this machine set the shift or the carrier.
    sound Play the machine like an instrument: harmonies from a single voice, or a ring modulator tuned to the keys.
Root        "Root"          0 127 60    int 0                                        | The note that means no shift (MIDI note, 60 = C4)
    id root
    how Sets the note at which Pitch mode does not shift; other notes shift by the distance from it.
    sound Play a fifth above the root and the sound moves up a fifth.
group Output
LowCut      "Low cut"       0 1000 0    freq 10 1000                                 | High-pass on the wet path
    id low_cut
    how Removes low frequencies from the shifted sound only.
    sound Takes the rumble out of a pitch-shifted-down sound.
HighCut     "High cut"      0 1000 1000 freq 1000 22000                              | Low-pass on the wet path
    id high_cut
    how Removes high frequencies from the shifted sound only.
    sound Takes the fizz and aliasing out of shifted-up and ring-modulated sounds.
Mix         "Mix"           0 1000 1000 pct                                          | Dry/wet (the dry signal is delayed by the latency)
    id mix
    how Blends the processed sound with the dry input.
    sound Lower values keep the original and lay the effect on top.
Amount      "Amount"        0 1000 500  lin 0 200 % 0                                | Effect strength: 100 % = the settings as they stand, 0 = clean (bit for bit the input), 200 % = twice the shift, fine shift, detune, feedback and spread
    id amount
    how Scales the pitch, the fine shift, the detune, the frequency shift, the feedback, the spread and the ring depth together.
    sound Turn it down to fade the effect out, up to push the shift twice as far; at 0 the sound is clean.
Output      "Output"        0 1000 500  db -24 24                                    | Output level of the wet sound
    id output
    how Sets the level of the processed sound.
    sound Pitch shifts and ring modulation change the loudness; trim it here.
